# Every data file is LF, in the index and in the working tree.
#
# Python's csv module writes CRLF by default — RFC 4180 says so — which means a
# script that rewrites one cell hands back a file where every line has changed.
# That happened twice: once to milestones.csv, once to events.csv, and both
# times the real one-line edit was invisible inside a whole-file diff.
#
# This is the belt. The braces are `lineterminator="\n"` wherever the code
# writes a CSV, and `test_data_files_are_lf`, which fails if one slips through.
*.csv text eol=lf

# The rest of the source, for the same reason and with less history behind it.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
